articles.text:
Following the letter of appointment published in the second number of The Contributor, for vol.

XII. (December 1890), Elder Milton H. Hardy began his special educational mission on Sunday, December 6th, 1890, at Salem and Mapleton, in Utah County.

On Sunday, December 14th, held two general public meetings and an officers'meeting at Nephi, Juab County.

Monday, 15th, two meetings at Levan;

and Tuesday, 16th, two meetings at Mona.

Thence to Spring City, Sanpete County, on the 17th; Mount Pleasant on the 18th;

Chester, 19th;

Fairview, 20th;

Ephraim and Manti on the 21st;

Mayfield, 22nd;

Gunnison, 23rd Fayette, 24th; thence to Juab and Provo on the 25th, At the Stake meetings the following subjects were presented and explained:

1. Organization—Stake Superintendency complete—operative.

2. Records a minutes b reports c finances.

3.

Circular letter from General Superintendency.

4. Stake council meetings.

5. Stake conferences: a annual or spring;

b semi-annual or fall.

6. Stake officers'meetings.

7. Stake recreations.

8.

Officers'visits.

9. The Contributor: a as a reference book;

b for general reading;

c for sending to friends.

10. Number of Associations in the Stake.

11. Number of young men in the Stake.

12. Number of members in the Associations.

13. Number of sets of Y. M. M.
